\f0\b\fs24 \cf0 CrystalLogoMoviePlayer API
\b0 \
\pard\tx566\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\ql\qnatural\pardirnatural
\cf0 \

\b Purpose:
\b0 \
\
The Crystal Logo Movie Player API is designed to be a quick and simple API for integrating the Chillingo movies into a developers project. \
\
The movie can be played in different orientations and the name of the movie can be specified allowing the developer to customise the movie being used.  Once the playback has started you can end the movie playback by tapping the screen or simply wait for it to finish.  Once complete the applications custom code can continue execution.\
\

\b Files:
\b0 \
\
CrystalLogoMoviePlayer.m and .h are the implementation of the movie player objective-c classes that make up the API\
\
CrystalAppDelegate.m and .h is an example app delegate incorporating the logo movie player that should be used as a guide for integrating the movie player into a developers application.\
\

\b How to integrate the logo movie player:
\b0 \
\
The following are the general steps required for setting up the logo movie player within an application:\
\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ql\qnatural
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}Make sure your logos are in the m4v format (currently this is the only format supported for playback) and add them to the application project\
{\listtext	\'95	}Add the CrystalLogoMoviePlayer files to the project and update your application delegate to implement the CrystalLogoMoviePlayerObserver protocol.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Implement the logoMovieDidFinish method (part of the observer protocol) where you can release the logo movie player and start the application as normal. \
{\listtext	\'95	}In the app delegates applicationDidFinishLaunching method\'a0create the logo movie player passing the appropriate parameters. There are three parameters for this:\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\ql\qnatural
\ls1\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	
\f1 \uc0\u9702 
\f0 	}movieName - the movie to play\
{\listtext	
\f1 \uc0\u9702 
\f0 	}orientation - the orientation you wish to play the movie in and should coincide with how the movie is recorded\
{\listtext	
\f1 \uc0\u9702 
\f0 	}observer - the app delegate in this case\'a0\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ql\qnatural
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}If you wish to use multiple movies in sequence then you could try the following\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\ql\qnatural
\ls1\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	
\f1 \uc0\u9702 
\f0 	}create a new movie player and use a counter to control which movie you are playing. \'a0When the counter reaches the required movie count then start your application code.\
{\listtext	
\f1 \uc0\u9702 
\f0 	}merge your movies into one big movie.  This may have consequences form a memory point of view however.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ql\qnatural
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}Once the movie player has been created via the app delegate code, trigger the start method to start the movie playback.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Once playback has finished or the user taps on the screen the observers logoMovieDidFinish method will be triggered allowing the application to continue as normal\
